r><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA TORU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA KOICHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIYAZAKI, HIROSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MIZUTANI, TERUYOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MORI, TATSUO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEDA, TORU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YAMASHITA, KOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An organic electroluminescent element comprising a pair of electrodes (2) and (5) at least one of which is transparent and, interposed therebetween, organic compound layers such as a hole injection layer (3) and a luminescent/electron injection layer (4), wherein at least one of the organic compound layers comprises a compound represented by general formula (1) wherein R1 to R12 each represents a substituent, e.g., alkyl, or hydrogen. The organic EL element is excellent in all of luminescent properties, reliability, and durability and is useful as a luminescent element in various displays.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un élément électroluminescent organique comprenant deux électrodes (2 et 5), au moins une de ces électrodes étant transparente, et des couches d'un composé organique intercalé entre les deux électrodes, par exemple une couche(3) à injection de trous et une couche (4) luminescente/à injection d'électrons. Au moins une de ces couches organiques comprend un composé représenté par la formule générale (1) dans laquelle R1 à R12 représentent chacun un substituant tel que l'alkyle ou l'hydrogène. L'élément organique électroluminescent présente d'excellentes propriétés de luminescence, de fiabilité et de durabilité, et convient en tant qu'élément luminescent pour divers dispositifs d'affichage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>